-- A subscription grants a plan by its product as well as its status, and its
-- version keeps the provider's microseconds (generated by drizzle-kit and
-- packages/db/scripts/rebuild-migration.mjs, then completed by hand).
--
-- `plan` is what the subscription's product grants its customer, null for a
-- product that grants none. Entitlement read status alone, so a customer who
-- switched to another product in Polar's portal kept the plan they left. Every
-- stored row was adopted with its customer's configured product, so each
-- starts on its customer's plan; the daily reconciliation rereads every live
-- subscription, and one whose product has changed since loses it then.
